BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w7-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
SUMMARY:OPTIONAL easy ride 60-75 min - the day after the long day. Zero i
 mpact. THIS IS THE FIRST THING TO CUT when work bites.
DESCRIPTION:Week 7 of 17 - Build\nRESET WEEK. Two corrections that change
  everything. (1) You have steep terrain 20-25 MINUTES away - Zuid-Kennem
 erland dunes by train\, faces at 30-45%. I told you the nearest hills we
 re 2.5-3 h\; that was wrong. (2) Your plan's vertical is an ORDER OF MAG
 NITUDE short: 40 min/week is ~400 m against a 2\,003 m race. From here e
 verything is measured in time and vertical metres\, never kilometres. LO
 CKED WEEK SHAPE: Sun optional easy ride - MON REST - TUE legs + precondi
 tioning walk ONLY (this is THE eccentric day - keep it focused\, no uppe
 r) - WED easy run + strides + push - THU vertical + pull - FRI REST - SA
 T LONG DAY. Eccentric work sits 48 h apart throughout: Tue heavy\, Thu m
 oderate\, Sat long. That spacing is the constraint - force loss needs 3 
 days to recover and soreness 4\, so 24 h between eccentric sessions comp
 ounds damage instead of building tolerance. Cutbacks weeks 10 and 13. CU
 T ORDER: (1) Sunday ride\, (2) Thursday vertical. Never Saturday's long 
 day or Tuesday's legs. HYROX SEEDING STARTS: only via substitution insid
 e Thursday's pull session - erg warm-up\, farmers carry\, dead hangs. NO
 T wall balls\, sandbag lunges or burpee broad jumps - those are all quad
  and eccentric load competing directly with the descent block. NOT compr
 omised running - it breaks the 80/20 distribution Madeira needs. The poi
 nt is to arrive in November with technique and grip already built\, so t
 he first two Hyrox weeks are productive instead of remedial.\n77 days to
  Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w7-s1-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260819
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:Easy run 6 km (talk test) + 6-8 x 20 s strides after (relaxed\, f
 ull recovery\, not a workout)
DESCRIPTION:Week 7 of 17 - Build\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Tal
 k test.\nRESET WEEK. Two corrections that change everything. (1) You hav
 e steep terrain 20-25 MINUTES away - Zuid-Kennemerland dunes by train\, 
 faces at 30-45%. I told you the nearest hills were 2.5-3 h\; that was wr
 ong. (2) Your plan's vertical is an ORDER OF MAGNITUDE short: 40 min/wee
 k is ~400 m against a 2\,003 m race. From here everything is measured in
  time and vertical metres\, never kilometres. LOCKED WEEK SHAPE: Sun opt
 ional easy ride - MON REST - TUE legs + preconditioning walk ONLY (this 
 is THE eccentric day - keep it focused\, no upper) - WED easy run + stri
 des + push - THU vertical + pull - FRI REST - SAT LONG DAY. Eccentric wo
 rk sits 48 h apart throughout: Tue heavy\, Thu moderate\, Sat long. That
  spacing is the constraint - force loss needs 3 days to recover and sore
 ness 4\, so 24 h between eccentric sessions compounds damage instead of 
 building tolerance. Cutbacks weeks 10 and 13. CUT ORDER: (1) Sunday ride
 \, (2) Thursday vertical. Never Saturday's long day or Tuesday's legs. H
 YROX SEEDING STARTS: only via substitution inside Thursday's pull sessio
 n - erg warm-up\, farmers carry\, dead hangs. NOT wall balls\, sandbag l
 unges or burpee broad jumps - those are all quad and eccentric load comp
 eting directly with the descent block. NOT compromised running - it brea
 ks the 80/20 distribution Madeira needs. The point is to arrive in Novem
 ber with technique and grip already built\, so the first two Hyrox weeks
  are productive instead of remedial.\n74 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w7-s2-push@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260819
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260820
SUMMARY:Push (upper) - after the easy run. Fresh\, not on legs you just d
 estroyed.
DESCRIPTION:Week 7 of 17 - Build\nRESET WEEK. Two corrections that change
  everything. (1) You have steep terrain 20-25 MINUTES away - Zuid-Kennem
 erland dunes by train\, faces at 30-45%. I told you the nearest hills we
 re 2.5-3 h\; that was wrong. (2) Your plan's vertical is an ORDER OF MAG
 NITUDE short: 40 min/week is ~400 m against a 2\,003 m race. From here e
 verything is measured in time and vertical metres\, never kilometres. LO
 CKED WEEK SHAPE: Sun optional easy ride - MON REST - TUE legs + precondi
 tioning walk ONLY (this is THE eccentric day - keep it focused\, no uppe
 r) - WED easy run + strides + push - THU vertical + pull - FRI REST - SA
 T LONG DAY. Eccentric work sits 48 h apart throughout: Tue heavy\, Thu m
 oderate\, Sat long. That spacing is the constraint - force loss needs 3 
 days to recover and soreness 4\, so 24 h between eccentric sessions comp
 ounds damage instead of building tolerance. Cutbacks weeks 10 and 13. CU
 T ORDER: (1) Sunday ride\, (2) Thursday vertical. Never Saturday's long 
 day or Tuesday's legs. HYROX SEEDING STARTS: only via substitution insid
 e Thursday's pull session - erg warm-up\, farmers carry\, dead hangs. NO
 T wall balls\, sandbag lunges or burpee broad jumps - those are all quad
  and eccentric load competing directly with the descent block. NOT compr
 omised running - it breaks the 80/20 distribution Madeira needs. The poi
 nt is to arrive in November with technique and grip already built\, so t
 he first two Hyrox weeks are productive instead of remedial.\n74 days to
  Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
