UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w7-s3-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260818
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260819
SUMMARY:Legs ONLY\, no upper - heavy eccentric. Decline squat 3-5 x 3-6 a
 t 80%+ 1RM\, step-downs 3 x 8-10/leg with 3-4 s lowering\, Nordics 3 x 5
 \, single-leg calf raises. Never to failure. 48-72 h before the long day
 . Add hip abductors - side plank raises\, banded lateral walks\, single-
 leg hip drops. On a -15% descent hip drop is 23.7 mm vs 7.6 mm uphill (v
 ery large effect). Descending is a frontal-plane hip problem\, not just 
 a quad problem. HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65
 % load (~100 kg)\, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Fore
 arms hooked on the posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm 
 at 3-4 per second\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CON
 CENTRIC\, so it costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is th
 e one Hyrox station you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweigh
 t of horizontal force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep on
 e rolling\, so learning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone 
 heavier. About 8 minutes.
