BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w10-s3-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260909
SUMMARY:Legs ONLY\, no upper - maintenance. Volume down\, load held at 80
 %+ 1RM. HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (
 ~100 kg)\, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hoo
 ked on the posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 p
 er second\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\
 , so it costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hy
 rox station you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of hor
 izontal force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rollin
 g\, so learning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier.
  About 8 minutes.
DESCRIPTION:Week 10 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volum
 e.\nCutback. Deliberate\, and the reason matters: in trail runners\, inj
 ury weeks were preceded by load DROPPING 16-24% then rebounding 15-37%. 
 Yo-yo loading\, not absolute load\, is what precedes injury. This dip is
  planned and the rebound is controlled.\n54 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
