SUMMARY:ZIG-ZAG AND WET-ROCK PRACTICE 45 min. Traversing at 60 deg to the
  fall line halves the gradient\, 28% -> 14%. Wet volcanic rock and wet w
 ooden steps sit at friction 0.3-0.5 - barely enough to stand on a 28% sl
 ope\, let alone brake. In the wet\, zig-zagging and side-stepping are te
 chnique\, not cowardice.
DESCRIPTION:Week 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000
 -2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rat
 e FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace of
 f knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n42 days to U
 ltra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w12-s8-descent@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:PRECONDITIONING DOWNHILL WALK - 5 minutes\, 5.6 kg in the pack\, 
 walking DOWN stairs. Lift up\, walk down\, repeat for 5 min. ~110 m of d
 escent\, about 37 flights. One bout cuts strength loss 49%\, CK 47%\, so
 reness 66% a week later. Five minutes\, in your own building\, no travel
 .
DESCRIPTION:Week 12 of 17 - Build\nBiggest vertical week so far\, ~2\,000
 -2\,300 m. HR is now unreliable as a guide: in mountain ultras heart rat
 e FALLS ~34 bpm across the race while RPE rises from 4.3 to 6.9. Pace of
 f knee-extensor RPE - how your quads feel - not the watch.\n40 days to U
 ltra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260927
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260928
SUMMARY:OPTIONAL easy ride 60-75 min - the day after the long day. Zero i
 mpact. THIS IS THE FIRST THING TO CUT when work bites.
DESCRIPTION:Week 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volum
 e.\nCutback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM 
 you need at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is counted - peak-week day
 s run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most lik
 ely route to a stress fracture\, and your body mass must not trend down.
 \n35 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s1-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Easy run 6 km (talk test) + 6-8 x 20 s strides after (relaxed\, f
 ull recovery\, not a workout)
DESCRIPTION:Week 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volum
 e.\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Talk test.\nCutback before the t
 wo biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM you need at least 2\,250
  kcal before exercise is counted - peak-week days run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal
 . Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most likely route to a stress fr
 acture\, and your body mass must not trend down.\n32 days to Ultra X Mad
 eira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
