BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s3-legs@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260929
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260930
SUMMARY:Legs ONLY\, no upper - maintenance. Volume down\, load held at 80
 %+ 1RM. HYROX SLED TECHNIQUE at the end\, 8-10 x 12.5 m at 50-65% load (
 ~100 kg)\, 60-90 s rest. TECHNIQUE ONLY\, never to fatigue. Forearms hoo
 ked on the posts\, 30-45 deg lean\, short choppy steps 20-30 cm at 3-4 p
 er second\, and never let the sled stop. Sled push is PURELY CONCENTRIC\
 , so it costs your descent block nothing - which is why it is the one Hy
 rox station you can train now. At 56 kg you need 1.03x bodyweight of hor
 izontal force to break a stationary sled versus 0.81x to keep one rollin
 g\, so learning not to stop is worth more to you than to anyone heavier.
  About 8 minutes.
DESCRIPTION:Week 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volum
 e.\nCutback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM 
 you need at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is counted - peak-week day
 s run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most lik
 ely route to a stress fracture\, and your body mass must not trend down.
 \n33 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s4-vertical@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:VERTICAL 45 min - STAIRWELL\, your own building or a car park. ~1
 2 x 15 floors\, about 540 m. Lift up\, WALK DOWN - the descent is the po
 int. Dutch stair pitch is 30-33 deg\, inside the optimal climbing range\
 , and Madeira is full of stone staircases. Zero travel\, weather-proof.
DESCRIPTION:Week 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volum
 e.\nCutback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM 
 you need at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is counted - peak-week day
 s run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most lik
 ely route to a stress fracture\, and your body mass must not trend down.
 \n31 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w13-s5-pull@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261001
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261002
SUMMARY:Pull (upper) - after the vertical session. HYROX SEEDING\, all su
 bstitutions not additions: (1) WARM UP ON THE SKIERG OR ROWER\, 5-8 min\
 , technique only - hinge and drive the first third of the pull\, that is
  where 80% of ski power comes from. Replaces your normal warm-up\, costs
  nothing. (2) SWAP one row variation for a HEAVY FARMERS CARRY\, 4 x 40-
 60 m. Same pulling pattern\, direct Hyrox transfer. (3) Finish with DEAD
  HANGS\, 2-3 x max\, target 90 s by October. Grip takes 4-6 weeks to cha
 nge and it is what limits the farmers carry. About 3 minutes total added
  to the session.
DESCRIPTION:Week 13 of 17 - Build\nDOWN WEEK - recover\, do not add volum
 e.\nCutback before the two biggest weeks. Eat. At 56 kg with ~50 kg FFM 
 you need at least 2\,250 kcal before exercise is counted - peak-week day
 s run 4\,800-5\,000 kcal. Under-fuelling an 11-week ramp is the most lik
 ely route to a stress fracture\, and your body mass must not trend down.
 \n31 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
