BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w14-s0-cycling@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261004
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261005
SUMMARY:OPTIONAL easy ride 60-75 min - the day after the long day. Zero i
 mpact. THIS IS THE FIRST THING TO CUT when work bites.
DESCRIPTION:Week 14 of 17 - Peak\nTERRAIN WEEKEND #2 - POSBANK AGAIN\, no
 t the Ardennes. Roughly EUR 30 of petrol against EUR 200\, and twenty re
 ps of a 90-110 m climb is 1\,800 m of ascent AND hard-surface descent - 
 close to the whole race. Sustained descending on firm ground is the one 
 thing stairs cannot replicate\, and it is what decides your day. POLES: 
 bought 18-20 Sep\, so you have had three weeks on them by now. Use them 
 the whole session. They cut RPE 14-18% and measurably reduce muscle dama
 ge over a climb-and-descent day - but an inexperienced pole user in a fi
 eld study actually got SLOWER\, so the practice is the point. KIT-CHECK 
 HABIT STARTS HERE: every food item must be labelled with its calorie cou
 nt\, and all disposable packaging must carry your bib number. Tape a str
 ip on your gel flask reading contents and total kcal (e.g. '4x Upfront G
 el PRO - 640 kcal'). Do it from this session on\, not at registration.\n
 28 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
