SUMMARY:PEAK LONG DAY 3:45-4:00\, 1\,600-1\,800 m vert. Race kit\, poles\
 , race fuelling\, race shoes. Alternate 20-25 min climbing with 15-20 mi
 n flat to rehearse the sawtooth. DESCENT CUE: shorten the step\, 185-195
  spm. Understriding cut strength loss to -8.8% vs -15.5% at preferred st
 ep length - roughly halved. Do NOT coach foot strike: the more anterior 
 the strike\, the LARGER the quad torque loss. Let the terrain dictate it
 . (24 km)
DESCRIPTION:Week 15 of 17 - Peak\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Tal
 k test.\nPEAK WEEKEND - Sat 17 Oct\, 15 days out. This is the overload t
 he taper is built on\; the evidence favours peaking 14-15 days out\, not
