BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w17-s0-easy@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261026
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261027
SUMMARY:Easy shakeout 5 km
DESCRIPTION:Week 17 of 17 - Race\nKeep HR under 158. Walk the climbs. Tal
 k test.\nRACE WEEK. Sunday 1 Nov\, Calhau de Sao Jorge to Machico. THE S
 TART IS 11:00\, NOT DAWN - sunset is 18:17 and civil twilight ends 18:41
 . A 6:30 finish is daylight\; 7:00 is dusk\; 7:30 is DARK on exposed cli
 ff paths. YOUR HEADTORCH IS SAFETY KIT\, NOT A FORMALITY - carry it char
 ged. The late start also gives you an unhurried fuelling morning: eat pr
 operly\, this is an advantage. CHECKPOINTS ARE WATER ONLY - the 'water a
 nd snacks' line is wrong. Carry 420-490 g of carbohydrate yourself (~13 
 gels plus mix) across three ~2h10 legs\, roughly 2.6 kg of vest. Only ~2
  checkpoints\, ~10 km apart. KIT: 1.5 L hydration capacity\, taped-seam 
 hooded waterproof\, emergency blanket\, 800 kcal reserve\, phone with GP
 X\, spare warm layer\, and a BEAKER of at least 15 cl - bottles and flas
 ks are explicitly not accepted. Checks are enforced. CALIBRATION from th
 e 2025 field (n=34): winner 3:02:21\, median 5:24:37 (13.0 min/km)\, las
 t finisher 8:03:43\, cut-off 11.5 h. Your target is 6:15-6:45. The 25K i
 s the final 25 km of the 50K route - the organiser gave the SHORT race t
 he STEEPEST ground\, 80 m/km against 63.5 for the 50K. PACING - the sing
 le strongest result in the literature (n=23\,207): in 91% of races\, slo
 wer finishers overspent in the FIRST segment\; after the opening everyon
 e paces the rest alike. The damage is done at the start. Hike every grad
 ient above 15% from the gun. HR: race average 138-150\, climb ceiling 15
 5\, descents 120-140. Above 160 for two minutes on a climb\, walk. Your 
 17 km run averaged 163 - you cannot hold that for six hours. THE DESCENT
  IS THE RACE. Racing the first steep descent saves ~10 minutes and costs
  17-46 minutes later: 3:1 to 5:1 against\, before you count the fall ris
 k. And it will never feel hard - VO2 on descents is only 79% of threshol
 d versus 100% uphill\, so your breathing will tell you nothing. That is 
 the trap. Short steps\, 185-195 spm\, gaze 4-5 m ahead on the second upc
 oming foothold\, walk the stone staircases\, zig-zag the wet sections. I
 N-RACE DIAGNOSTIC: compare climb rate per heartbeat on the second climb 
 against the first. More than 5% worse means you overcooked the descent -
  concede ten minutes immediately and save the day. FUEL: 60-75 g/h at 2:
 1 glucose:fructose\, drink to thirst\, skip the salt capsules (no eviden
 ce they prevent hyponatraemia or cramp). Carb load 8-10 g/kg for 36-48 h
  = 450-560 g. Caffeine ~100 mg at 3 h and 75-100 mg at 4.5 h\, 150-200 m
 g total - do not scale from 70 kg examples. WEATHER: use Santana on the 
 north coast\, not Funchal - 18 C max\, 110 mm of rain across ~40% of day
 s. Wet basalt and hypothermia are the risks here\, not heat. Bib pickup 
 Fri 30 Oct or Sat 31 Oct\, 18:00-20:00\, Machico Forum. No crew\, no pac
 ers\, no drop bags.\n6 days to Ultra X Madeira 25K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ultraxmadeira25k-w17-s1-strides@garmin-training
DTSTAMP:20260818T134501Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261028
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261029
SUMMARY:Easy 3-4 km + 4 x 90 s at race-climb effort. Do not skip this.
DESCRIPTION:Week 17 of 17 - Race\nRACE WEEK. Sunday 1 Nov\, Calhau de Sao
  Jorge to Machico. THE START IS 11:00\, NOT DAWN - sunset is 18:17 and c
 ivil twilight ends 18:41. A 6:30 finish is daylight\; 7:00 is dusk\; 7:3
 0 is DARK on exposed cliff paths. YOUR HEADTORCH IS SAFETY KIT\, NOT A F
 ORMALITY - carry it charged. The late start also gives you an unhurried 
 fuelling morning: eat properly\, this is an advantage. CHECKPOINTS ARE W
 ATER ONLY - the 'water and snacks' line is wrong. Carry 420-490 g of car
 bohydrate yourself (~13 gels plus mix) across three ~2h10 legs\, roughly
  2.6 kg of vest. Only ~2 checkpoints\, ~10 km apart. KIT: 1.5 L hydratio
 n capacity\, taped-seam hooded waterproof\, emergency blanket\, 800 kcal
  reserve\, phone with GPX\, spare warm layer\, and a BEAKER of at least 
 15 cl - bottles and flasks are explicitly not accepted. Checks are enfor
 ced. CALIBRATION from the 2025 field (n=34): winner 3:02:21\, median 5:2
 4:37 (13.0 min/km)\, last finisher 8:03:43\, cut-off 11.5 h. Your target
  is 6:15-6:45. The 25K is the final 25 km of the 50K route - the organis
 er gave the SHORT race the STEEPEST ground\, 80 m/km against 63.5 for th
 e 50K. PACING - the single strongest result in the literature (n=23\,207
 ): in 91% of races\, slower finishers overspent in the FIRST segment\; a
 fter the opening everyone paces the rest alike. The damage is done at th
 e start. Hike every gradient above 15% from the gun. HR: race average 13
 8-150\, climb ceiling 155\, descents 120-140. Above 160 for two minutes 
 on a climb\, walk. Your 17 km run averaged 163 - you cannot hold that fo
 r six hours. THE DESCENT IS THE RACE. Racing the first steep descent sav
 es ~10 minutes and costs 17-46 minutes later: 3:1 to 5:1 against\, befor
 e you count the fall risk. And it will never feel hard - VO2 on descents
  is only 79% of threshold versus 100% uphill\, so your breathing will te
 ll you nothing. That is the trap. Short steps\, 185-195 spm\, gaze 4-5 m
  ahead on the second upcoming foothold\, walk the stone staircases\, zig
 -zag the wet sections. IN-RACE DIAGNOSTIC: compare climb rate per heartb
 eat on the second climb against the first. More than 5% worse means you 
 overcooked the descent - concede ten minutes immediately and save the da
 y. FUEL: 60-75 g/h at 2:1 glucose:fructose\, drink to thirst\, skip the 
 salt capsules (no evidence they prevent hyponatraemia or cramp). Carb lo
 ad 8-10 g/kg for 36-48 h = 450-560 g. Caffeine ~100 mg at 3 h and 75-100
  mg at 4.5 h\, 150-200 mg total - do not scale from 70 kg examples. WEAT
 HER: use Santana on the north coast\, not Funchal - 18 C max\, 110 mm of
  rain across ~40% of days. Wet basalt and hypothermia are the risks here
 \, not heat. Bib pickup Fri 30 Oct or Sat 31 Oct\, 18:00-20:00\, Machico
  Forum. No crew\, no pacers\, no drop bags.\n4 days to Ultra X Madeira 2
 5K.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
